\par\par \uc2 AtHome; SECTD\par \b \uc2 Don't Forget, the Boss Could Be Watching\b0\par\par\uc2 By Thorin Klosowski \par \uc2 288 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 February 2021\par \uc2 The New York Times\par \uc2 NYTF\par \uc2 Late Edition - Final\par 4\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 The New York Times Company.  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 If you're working from home, chances are you're using a work-issued laptop, employer-owned communication tools or software to remotely gain access to the servers at the office. And in some cases, remote work tools also give your boss tools for surveillance. Here's what to know.\par \par \uc2 Work tools like Slack and email are often monitored by employers, but there are typically barriers between the administrator and management. Still, anything you say using those programs is viewable by the company, so take private conversations to a different device.\par \par \uc2 Avoid using employer-operated cloud storage like Google Docs or Office 365 to store personal files. Some employers use monitoring tools to flag file names like ''resume.docx,'' to track employees as a flight risk, and files you store would be inaccessible if you quit or get fired, anyway.\par \par \uc2 If you log in to your office computer through a remote desktop tool, or use an employer-provided virtual private network or VPN, it's like working from your office desk. Don't browse sketchy websites, even in an incognito window.\par \par \uc2 Monitoring software (''bossware'') is custom software employers can install to monitor everything you do on your computer, taking snapshots of your screen or providing dashboards showing how you spend your time. It can be invisible, so avoid doing personal business altogether on a company device.\par \par \uc2 For peace of mind, you could ask your employer what information it collects from your work computer. You could also ask under what circumstances your employer would go through the steps of looking at the data.\par \par \uc2 Adapted from Wirecutter, the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  company that reviews and recommends products.\par \par \uc2 Document NYTF000020210214eh2e00063\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw284\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal4260\pichgoal600
