\par\par \uc2 Business/Financial Desk; SECTB\par \b \uc2 The Digest\b0\par\par\uc2 By Jack Ewing, Reuters and Katie Robertson \par \uc2 479 \uc2 words\par \uc2 22 January 2021\par \uc2 The New York Times\par \uc2 NYTF\par \uc2 Late Edition - Final\par 2\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 The New York Times Company.  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 EMISSIONS\par \par \uc2 Volkswagen\uc2  Faces Fine After Missing Targets\par \par \uc2 Volkswagen\uc2 , the largest carmaker in Europe, faces penalties of more than 100 million euros, or $120 million, after it failed last year to cut the carbon dioxide emissions of its vehicles enough to meet European standards.\par \par \uc2 The company blamed sluggish auto sales caused by the pandemic for the disruption, which slowed the rollout of its new electric vehicle, the ID.3.\par \par \uc2 Still, the failure to meet environmental standards was a setback as \uc2 Volkswagen\uc2  tries to position itself as the company that will make electric cars affordable. The German company is still recovering from an emissions cheating scandal in 2015 that badly damaged its reputation.\par \par \uc2 European Union\uc2  rules that took effect last year compel carmakers to sharply reduce their output of carbon dioxide, a cause of climate change. \uc2 Volkswagen\uc2  said that it cut average CO2 emissions of its vehicles by 20 percent compared with 2019, but that was not enough to avoid penalties. JACK EWING\par \par \uc2 RAILROADS\par \par \uc2 Higher Shipping Volume Buoys Union Pacific\par \par \uc2 The freight operator Union Pacific reported better-than-expected quarterly profit on Thursday, bolstered by higher shipping volumes of grain, refrigerated food and drinks, and retail goods.\par \par \uc2 Still, shares in the company fell 4.3 percent to $208.85 in midday trading on concern that the pace of volume growth and efficiency gains could moderate as a slow vaccine rollout threatens an economy battered by the Covid-19 pandemic.\par \par \uc2 Union Pacific\uc2 , which ferries goods in and out of busy seaports, expects 2021 volume growth of 4-6 percent.\par \par \uc2 Analysts expect the recovery in U.S. railroad volumes to continue in 2021, with a pickup in demand giving way to broader-based gains in rail traffic, spurred by wood products for home construction, grains for biofuels and export to China, and goods sold via ecommerce.\par \par \uc2 Chief Executive \uc2 Lance Fritz\uc2  said \uc2 Union Pacific\uc2  would adapt to whatever 2021 brings. REUTERS\par \par \uc2 MEDIA\par \par \uc2 New Yorker Fact Checkers Stage a One-Day Walkout\par \par \uc2 The more than 100 employees represented by The New Yorker Union, which includes fact checkers, web producers and some other editorial employees, staged a daylong walkout on Thursday after recent rounds of negotiations with management failed, said Natalie Meade, the union chair.\par \par \uc2 Ms. Meade said the company did not hit the union's $65,000 minimum salary demand, instead offering wage increases she called ''insulting.'' In a statement, a spokesperson said the company's most recent proposals were ''initial offers.''\par \par \uc2 In September, Senator Elizabeth Warren, Democrat of Massachusetts, and Representative Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez, Democrat of New York, pulled out of keynote speaker slots at The New Yorker Festival in solidarity with union workers, who were planning a digital picket line to pressure management into including a ''just cause'' proposal in their agreement. KATIE ROBERTSON\par \par \uc2 (PHOTOGRAPH BY NATI HARNIK/ASSOCIATED PRESS) \par \par \uc2 Document NYTF000020210122eh1m0005p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw284\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal4260\pichgoal600
